on fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\n\r\nThe network fields indicate where a remote logon request originated. Workstation name is not always available and may be left blank in some cases.\r\n\r\nThe impersonation level field indicates the extent to which a process in the logon session can impersonate.\r\n\r\nThe authentication information fields provide detailed information about this specific logon request.\r\n\t- Logon GUID is a unique identifier that can be used to correlate this event with a KDC event.\r\n\t- Transited services indicate which intermediate services have participated in this logon request.\r\n\t- Package name indicates which sub-protocol was used among the NTLM protocols.\r\n\t- Key length indicates the length of the generated session key. This will be 0 if no session key was requested.","Category":"Logon","Opcode":"Info","SubjectUserSid":"S-1-0-0","SubjectUserName":"-","SubjectDomainName":"-","SubjectLogonId":"0x0","TargetUserSid":"S-1-5-18","TargetUserName":"ACTIVEDIR$","TargetDomainName":"STACKEDPADS.LOCAL","TargetLogonId":"0x1df011","LogonType":"3","LogonProcessName":"Kerberos","AuthenticationPackageName":"Kerberos","WorkstationName":"-","LogonGuid":"{d653b585-a935-c867-4f5a-3aa42abbe6ce}","TransmittedServices":"-","LmPackageName":"-","KeyLength":"0","ProcessName":"-","IpAddress":"::1","IpPort":"49841","ImpersonationLevel":"%%1833","RestrictedAdminMode":"-","TargetOutboundUserName":"-","TargetOutboundDomainName":"-","VirtualAccount":"%%1843","TargetLinkedLogonId":"0x0","ElevatedToken":"%%1842","EventReceivedTime":1657288168,"SourceModuleName":"in_default_channels","SourceModuleType":"im_msvistalog"}
