ges removed and administrative groups disabled.  The limited token is used when User Account Control is enabled, the application does not require administrative privilege, and the user does not choose to start the program using Run as administrator.","Category":"Process Creation","Opcode":"Info","SubjectUserSid":"S-1-5-19","SubjectUserName":"LOCAL SERVICE","SubjectDomainName":"NT AUTHORITY","SubjectLogonId":"0x3e5","NewProcessId":"0x11b4","NewProcessName":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\audiodg.exe","TokenElevationType":"%%1936","CommandLine":"C:\\Windows\\system32\\AUDIODG.EXE 0x3b0 0x3ac","TargetUserSid":"S-1-0-0","TargetUserName":"-","TargetDomainName":"-","TargetLogonId":"0x0","ParentProcessName":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe","MandatoryLabel":"S-1-16-16384","EventReceivedTime":1657289544,"SourceModuleName":"in_default_channels","SourceModuleType":"im_msvistalog"}
